+# UD gauge transport theorem v0.1
+
+EXACT CONDITIONAL finite mathematics; CANDIDATE physical extension. Development, no registry promotion. Independent review pending. Physical promotion 0.
+
+Read UD_GAUGE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf and its editable LaTeX source. The principal theorem defines norm-conserving, gauge-covariant transport on the 28 Hasse links of the 15-coordinate tetrahedron, proves its curvature/flatness boundary and gives an exact one-phase spectral corollary. These are scoped finite-model results using established gauge and connection mathematics, not Standard Model or GUT derivations.
+
+Replay with Python3 and SymPy:
+
+    python3 verify_hasse_transport.py
+    python3 verify_gauge_bridge.py
+
+The first is the primary Hasse-link checker (69 named checks). The second is a supporting, differently constructed ordered-vertex fixture and native symmetry/normalization checker (25 named checks). Counts are constructor verification, not independent confirmations or universal proofs. The manuscript contains the universal arguments, including an independent analytic Gram proof of the phase spectrum.
+
+The candidate state, readouts and missing action/physical gates are recorded in GAUGE_BRIDGE_CONTRACT_v0.1.json; typed claim scopes are in CLAIM_AND_BRIDGE_LEDGER_v0.1.json. Source file hashes and external primary references are in SOURCE_PROVENANCE_v0.1.json. No experimental data were fitted or scored. The supplied Genesis image remains unavailable and unused.
+
+Rebuild the A4 manuscript with two pdflatex passes. No archived research script is required. The original signed chain boundary remains unchanged; curved transport is a new covariant operator whose square has an explicit curvature defect.
