+# Gauge-covariant incidence transport: theorem milestone v0.1
+
+Status: EXACT CONDITIONAL finite mathematics; CANDIDATE physical bridge. Constructor verified; independent review pending; physical promotion 0. This is a dedicated theorem manuscript, separate from the narrative review candidate and the four source papers.
+
+## Result
+
+Assign a complex rank-r fiber to each of the 15 oriented tetrahedral simplex coordinates and a unitary map to each of the 28 adjacent incidence links. With D_U carrying the signed link blocks, A_U=D_U^dagger-D_U is skew-Hermitian. Local unitary frame changes, including their temporal connection term, preserve the evolution and gauge-invariant signed support currents. Signed S4 relabeling is covariance of the connection family, not invariance of every individual field configuration.
+
+The square D_U^2 measures the difference of the two transport paths around each incidence diamond. On the filled tetrahedron, demanding D_U^2=0 makes all such paths flat and the full connection pure gauge. Its instantaneous A_U spectrum is then just r copies of the native spectrum. This concerns incidence flatness; mixed temporal curvature can remain nonzero, and full time-dependent propagators need not agree. Curved transport is still norm conserving, with the exact relation -A_U^2=L_U-D_U^2-(D_U^dagger)^2. The original topological boundary B remains nilpotent; the curved covariant operator is a new object.
+
+## A constructive spectral corollary
+
+Set r=1 and change only the vertex0 <- edge01 link from 1 to exp(i phi), with unit magnitude throughout. The exact characteristic polynomial is
+
+    lambda (lambda^2+4)^5 [(lambda^2+4)^2 - 4(1-cos(phi))].
+
+At phi=pi/2 the nonzero positive frequencies are sqrt(2), 2, sqrt(6), with multiplicities 1, 5, 1; there is one zero mode. The manuscript proves this by a two-plane Gram reduction. Five exact phase cases are also verified computationally. This supports a conditional 15-mode analogue specification; it does not predict the Standard Model force couplings.
+
+## Symmetry and coupling boundary
+
+The native global orthogonal centralizer is O(1)xU(7); simultaneously commuting with signed S4 restricts it to O(1)xU(1)^3. This restriction is a declared branch, not a prohibition of enlarged or noncommuting gauge branches. Exact scalar phase receipts from one state have trivial closed products and cannot alone supply independent curvature.
+
+Even assuming su(3)+su(2)+u(1), positive invariant kinetic forms retain three independent coefficients. Simple-group matching and hypercharge normalization require additional premises; SU(5) is demonstrated only as a conditional standard normalization example. No group, matter, action or beta-function selection is inferred from equal counts or a shared frequency.
+
+## Verification and next gate
+
+69 primary exact Hasse-link checks and 25 supporting checks passed. They are constructor checks, not independent reviews. Written universal proofs accompany the finite fixtures. No experimental data were fitted or scored. Discrete connection/curvature mathematics is established background; no general novelty claim is made.
+
+Highest-value next construction: a closed joint link-matter action or phase-space law, including Gauss constraints, reciprocal backreaction and conserved total quantities. Then test locality, continuum/relativistic behavior and chiral matter before attempting renormalization-group matching. Physical group identification, clock/action units, proton operators, monopole sectors and independent physical correspondence remain OPEN.
